{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"salmon-abominable-pupa","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context\n\nCode review already routes changed Terraform to the `code-review-iac` overlay, but its Pass-1 overlay and Pass-2 verifier have only generic repository tools. This slice reuses the tool-session contract created by `forcible-diminished-lamb` [rebar:forcible-diminished-lamb] so IaC findings can cite and independently re-check whole-module evidence. It changes no behavior for other diffs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Thread `assemble_diff.outputs.changed_files` into `CodeReviewBatchRunner`; its constructor already stores this field, but the production gate dispatcher currently omits it.\n- In both Round A and Round B, create a fresh Terraform tool session only for an included `code-review-iac` criterion when the changed set contains `.tf`, `.tf.json`, or an explicitly changed `.tfvars`. Supply the `lookup_declaration` and `resolve_reference` tools from the prerequisite. The base reviewer and every other overlay receive no Terraform tools.\n- Scope the session from changed paths, then use the prerequisite's whole affected-module/local-closure rules. A changed `.tfvars` remains direct evidence only and is never treated as an automatically selected input.\n- After Pass-1 merge, expose a new session to `code-review-verify` only when a merged finding is attributed to `code-review-iac` and the changed set has Terraform scope. The verifier receives the Pass-1 receipt as evidence but must issue its own query; there is no inherited answer or query ledger.\n- The coach and deterministic decision steps receive no Terraform tools.\n- Merge concrete/module-membership reads into the call's `_usage.distinct_fetches`. Include the concrete Terraform files read in the code-review sidecar's reviewed-file `deps` so region-gated re-review memory cannot reuse evidence after a module dependency changes.\n- Keep missing-extra behavior fail-open: code review continues through its existing generic path, with no advertised Terraform tools. An advertised tool failure returns the prerequisite's closed abstention and cannot itself create or block a finding.\n- Do not add a scanner stage or originate findings from the index. The IaC overlay remains the finder; grounding only answers its explicit queries.\n\n## Positive rationale\n\nThe slice is independently releasable after its prerequisite: a Terraform diff receives query-grounded IaC review end to end, while all non-IaC requests remain byte-compatible. It reuses the existing overlay routing and generic per-call tool-provider seam instead of creating a Terraform-specific review engine.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nNo new parser, source-network logic, corroborator executable, prompt change, standalone validation, Terraform/OpenTofu/provider execution, or non-IaC tool exposure.\n\n## Failure-disposition contract\n\n- Missing `grounding-terraform` extra: non-fatal capability absence; advertise no tools and complete the ordinary review.\n- Unsupported/ambiguous/dynamic Terraform question: return ABSTAIN; the LLM may verify directly from files but the tool supplies no positive claim.\n- Parser/path/limit/timeout failure: return ABSTAIN and preserve the existing review result; do not reinterpret it as a clean module or nonexistent symbol.\n- Internal routing/session construction defect: surface through existing gate error handling rather than silently attaching tools to a broader step.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Production dispatch passes the exact assembled `changed_files` into `CodeReviewBatchRunner`, and a Round-A changed-`.tf` integration test observes both Terraform tools only on `code-review-iac`.\n- [ ] A Round-B escalation test observes the same tool surface and whole-module resolution when IaC is recommended rather than glob-selected, without running the overlay twice.\n- [ ] A merged IaC finding makes `code-review-verify` receive a distinct Terraform query session; a verifier tool call returns a fresh receipt rather than reusing the Pass-1 result.\n- [ ] Base review, non-IaC overlays, coach, a Python-only diff, and an IaC review with no IaC findings advertise no Terraform tools.\n- [ ] A changed `.tfvars` can be queried as direct structural evidence, and a test proves its value is not injected into module variables or used to resolve a computed reference.\n- [ ] Code-review usage and sidecar dependency tests contain the concrete sibling/local-module files read; modifying one invalidates the recorded dependency hash while an unrelated non-Terraform file does not.\n- [ ] Missing-extra and every prerequisite ABSTAIN outcome leave the ordinary code-review decision path intact and never become a synthetic IaC finding.\n\n## Testing\n\nTest contract card:\n\n- Authoritative contract: REB-640, this ticket, and the prerequisite's tool/receipt contract [rebar:forcible-diminished-lamb].\n- Preconditions: a real assembled diff with one changed root `.tf`, an unchanged sibling declaration, a local child module, and captured Round-A/Round-B/verifier requests.\n- Production path: production gate dispatch → real `CodeReviewBatchRunner` → real tool session; only the model result is faked.\n- Tier: workflow integration, because the contract crosses trigger selection, overlay batch dispatch, merge, verifier routing, usage, and sidecar dependency capture.\n- Oracle: exact tool-name sets per request, distinct receipt/query-session ids across passes, resolved sibling evidence, and changed dependency digest after editing a read file.\n- Negative controls: an equivalent `.py` diff and a Terraform diff with no IaC finding leave base/other overlays/verifier/coach tool-free.\n- CI: `make test`.\n\n## Verification\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py`","id":"afe3-5aec-51cb-4e02","parent_id":"a374-849c-c8f2-4234","priority":2,"tags":["terraform","grounding","llm","optional","code-review"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Ground code-review IaC findings in changed Terraform modules"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788469523116095726,"uuid":"e8287738-5c4a-4d08-a7fe-b20b4bf47631"}